#------------------------- PAR_DUMP -------------------------
<comment>
problem                                                                                                                             = He GIANT envelope before core collapse (MESA r15140 M2pt754_Porb100 profile29, Wu grid: M 2.556 Msun,                               
L_ph 1.62e4 Lsun, R_ph 61.78 Rsun, Teff 8.28 kK), FOLLOW THE EXPANSION. he_star_m1 on branch hegiant-1006:                          = L_ph 1.62e4 Lsun, R_ph 61.78 Rsun, Teff 8.28 kK), FOLLOW THE EXPANSION. he_star_m1 on branch hegiant-1006:                          
he_gm_column (enclosed-mass gravity of the IC column, static), he_base_heat (wall in the CZ: the                                    = he_gm_column (enclosed-mass gravity of the IC column, static), he_base_heat (wall in the CZ: the                                    
scaffold's wall luminosity L_MLT(3 Rsun) 6.72e6 Lsun stays as a 0.5 Rsun base heating layer). IC : MESA T(r) + HSE with our EOS and = scaffold's wall luminosity L_MLT(3 Rsun) 6.72e6 Lsun stays as a 0.5 Rsun base heating layer). IC : MESA T(r) + HSE with our EOS and 
our m(r) (ic/make_ic_giant_mesa.py --hse own), frozen MLT scaffold F - F_diff, RE atmosphere, floor 1e-20.                          = our m(r) (ic/make_ic_giant_mesa.py --hse own), frozen MLT scaffold F - F_diff, RE atmosphere, floor 1e-20.                          
General EOS X 0 Y 0.9265 (Z 0.0735 inert, a_metal 1.77 : fully ionized metals); TOPS tables of the                                  = General EOS X 0 Y 0.9265 (Z 0.0735 inert, a_metal 1.77 : fully ionized metals); TOPS tables of the                                  
envelope/surface mixtures blended in log T (tables/blend_tables.py). r 3-200 Rsun N445 (grid/fit_445:                               = envelope/surface mixtures blended in log T (tables/blend_tables.py). r 3-200 Rsun N445 (grid/fit_445:                               
dr : max(0.015 r, 0.15 Rsun) deep, plateau ~0.039 Rsun : H_atm/3 over 60.3-64.2 Rsun, dr/r <: 0.01 to                               = dr : max(0.015 r, 0.15 Rsun) deep, plateau ~0.039 Rsun : H_atm/3 over 60.3-64.2 Rsun, dr/r <: 0.01 to                               
130 Rsun). pi/3 x pi/3 wedge, 128 x 128 SCOUT layout (16 blocks 445 x 32 x 32). See SETUP.md.                                       = 130 Rsun). pi/3 x pi/3 wedge, 128 x 128 SCOUT layout (16 blocks 445 x 32 x 32). See SETUP.md.                                       
<job>
basename = hegiant 
<mesh>
nghost                    = 3                   
nx1                       = 897                 
x1min                     = 2.087100e11         # 3 Rsun
x1max                     = 1.391400e13         # 200 Rsun (outflow top; R_ph 61.78 Rsun at t : 0)
ix1_bc                    = user                
ox1_bc                    = user                
nx2                       = 128                 
x2min                     = 1.0471975511965976  # pi/3
x2max                     = 2.0943951023931953  # 2 pi/3
ix2_bc                    = periodic            
ox2_bc                    = periodic            
nx3                       = 128                 
x3min                     = 0.0                 
x3max                     = 1.0471975511965976  # pi/3
ix3_bc                    = periodic            
ox3_bc                    = periodic            
use_spherical_polar       = true                
use_grid_stretch_r_poly   = true                
f_stretch_r_c1            = -1.272273799858e+00 # grid/fit_giant.py 445 (DMIN 0.15): grid/fit_445.out
f_stretch_r_c2            = -1.977330494356e+01 
f_stretch_r_c3            = 2.926701797839e+02  
f_stretch_r_c4            = -1.484689926654e+03 
f_stretch_r_c5            = 3.739183469225e+03  
